<p>I'm gonna novote this SCP for now, mainly due to me not really understanding what's happening for the most part (or at least the Experiment Log 5633-█-█ part of the SCP).</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;My&nbsp;critique&nbsp;and&nbsp;issues</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;My&nbsp;critique&nbsp;and&nbsp;issues</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<ul>
<li>The formatting of the dates seem to switch around between Year/Month/Day, Month/Day/Year, and Day/Month/Year. I'd suggest to be consistent and only use 1 date format.</li>
<li>I think I understand that something changed history, but it started to get confusing as it went on. I can understand that there's time travel-wackery going on though.</li>
<li>The Experiment Log 5633-█-█ part specifically confuses me the most. To me, it seem to slowly not make sense.</li>
<li>You begin to introduce new instances of SCP-5633, but never really explain what they are. Like who or what are SCP-5633-β, SCP-5633-δ, SCP-5633-γ, and SCP-5633-Γ? When I was writing this, I thought that they could be Foundation members, but I don't think I got that until after.</li>
<li>I do like the ACS header, but it changes fairly quickly. I had to wait for it to go through a few times before I knew what each version said. I'd suggest slowing the switch speed of the header (assuming you can)</li>
</ul>
</div>
